  // EVERY PATH: Hana told Sam on Feb 17; the merger took effect Apr 3 under Corinne; the board's Mar 15 session footnoted the ARA's margin
  //   (UNDER BOARD REVIEW, July session); the manifest closed Jun 1 with all six bridge stacks; the blackout ran May 25 4:15 PM to Jun 16 11:04 PM
  //   Mountain time; the beacon showed MED 1 from Sol 4013 to 4019 and the director's line said STATION NOMINAL every sol; the first packet on
  //   Sat Jun 17 was the medical summary naming Ada (admitted Sol 4013, injured during oxygen plant repair; discharged Sol 4020, fit for light
  //   duty; clinical detail restricted). Sam's envelope to Ruth is still unsealed under his keys.
  closing:(s,all,G)=>{const p=s.picks||{}, rosy=p[11]===0, sac=s.flags.sacrificedhana;
    return [
    `Thursday, May 25. 4:15 PM. Quinn had the elongation up on the big screen in the program room, refreshing every five minutes from the agency's feed, and people had drifted in from both buildings without anybody calling them. 3.0026. 3.0017. 3.0008. At 4:15 it said 2.9999, and the relay network's personal queue changed from OPEN to CLOSED in small gray letters, and nobody said anything. Wendell had come in from the stand for no reason he'd give. <span class="said" data-who="Wendell">"Copy,"</span> he said, to nobody.`,
    (p[11]===3
      ?`Sam's own slot had closed at two with nothing in it from him. He'd sat at the kitchen table at 1:15 with the red light on for a long time and then turned it off.`
      :p[11]===2
        ?`He'd sent the monthly report at 1:52. It was accurate. It didn't have him in it.`
      :rosy
        ?`His log had gone at 1:52. He knew what was in it. So, by now, did she.`
        :`His log had gone at 1:52. It was the first one in a long while that he hadn't watched back twice.`),
    `The beacon came through the next morning on its second try. It was one line, and it would be one line every sol for twenty two days.`,
    `<prop type="doc" title="ARES STATION · STATUS BEACON · SOL 4005">PLANT GREEN · POWER GREEN · ECLSS GREEN · MED 0 · DIRECTOR: STATION NOMINAL</prop>`,
    (p[10]===2
      ?`The program posted it unedited at 7:12, as he'd told the families it would, and every morning after that. Frances sent him a photograph of it on her refrigerator, held up by a magnet shaped like Colorado.`
      :`The agency's public affairs office posted a summary of it on Fridays, in a paragraph that began with the word continues.`),
    `Thursday, June 1. The cargo manifest closed at noon with six RP-55 bridge stacks on it, 430 kilograms with their mounts, `+(p[8]===3?`and the station's sign off attached, dated May 19.`:`and a line at the bottom that said STATION CONFIRMATION TO FOLLOW.`),
    `Saturday, June 3. Sol 4013. He read the beacon at 6:20 in the kitchen, standing up.`,
    `<prop type="doc" title="ARES STATION · STATUS BEACON · SOL 4013">PLANT AMBER · POWER GREEN · ECLSS GREEN · MED 1 · DIRECTOR: STATION NOMINAL</prop>`,
    `The next sol the plant word was green again. One sol of amber wasn't a trigger, `+(p[9]===0?`by the matrix he'd written himself, and he'd written it that way on purpose, and he read the line in the matrix four times anyway.`:`and nobody had written down what would be.`)+` MED said 1 for seven sols. Two hundred and twelve people. <b>It's always somebody's ankle.</b> He didn't call anybody, because there was nobody to call who knew more than the beacon did. `+(p[10]===2?`At nine Frances called him. <span class="said" data-who="Frances">"I saw it."</span> <span class="said" data-who="Sam">"So did I."</span> They stayed on the line for a while without saying much.`:`Nobody called him either.`),
    `Monday, June 5. 10:00 PM. As close as it would get: from Earth, Mars was a little under half a degree from the middle of the Sun, a sliver of sky away from its edge. He sat at the kitchen table and recorded a log that wouldn't go anywhere for eleven days. `+(rosy
      ?`He told the recorder what he hadn't told her on Thursday: that the valve's root cause was still open, that the margin had two numbers, that he'd done the voice. It would reach her after she'd had three weeks with the other one. He recorded it anyway.`
      :`He told her about `+(p[2]===0?`Arlo's capitals on the high bay whiteboard`:`the coffee can on the stand console`)+`, and the candles in the jars at the gate, and that he'd read the beacon every morning standing up. He didn't do the voice. There was nobody to do it for.`),
    `Monday, June 12. Twenty seven years since the Petrel. He recorded the second log at eight, with page nine on the table and the envelope still under his keys by the door, still addressed to Ruth, still not sealed. He didn't tell Ada whose page it was. He told her that a woman he knew had once told a commander yes when the true answer was I don't know, and that he was trying to learn to say the true one.`,
    (sac
      ?`Hana came in at six every morning, as before. She hadn't asked anybody a question in a meeting since March.`
      :p[0]===1
        ?`At the root cause meeting that afternoon the agency's reviewer sent Hana the first written comments. <b>Your data are good. Your filing system is a crime.</b> Hana read it out loud, and the room laughed, and Arlo laughed loudest.`
        :p[0]===2
        ?`The root cause team met without her, as it had since February.`
        :`At the root cause meeting that afternoon Hana ran the data, as she always did, and nobody mentioned 2059, which was progress of a kind.`),
    (s.score>=27
      ?`He made a list in the notebook of what had held since February. It was longer than the other list. Ray would have told him to read it out loud. He read it to the kitchen.`
      :`He made a list in the notebook of what he'd do differently since February. It was getting easier to write, which he didn't think was the same as getting better.`),
    `Friday, June 16. 11:04 PM. The line passed. Nothing happened, because nothing could happen for at least twenty one minutes, and then the station would have to notice, and then the queue would have to drain. He was awake. He'd known he would be.`,
    `Saturday, June 17. 12:31 AM. The two note chime, for the first time in twenty two days. It wasn't a log.`,
    `<prop type="doc" title="ARES STATION · MEDICAL · CONJUNCTION SUMMARY · SOL 4005 TO SOL 4027">ADMISSIONS: 1.<br>OKAFOR, ADA. HYDROPONICS.<br>ADMITTED SOL 4013. INJURIES SUSTAINED DURING OXYGEN PLANT REPAIR.<br>DISCHARGED SOL 4020. FIT FOR LIGHT DUTY.<br>CLINICAL DETAIL: RESTRICTED. RELEASE TO NEXT OF KIN ON REQUEST.</prop>`,
    `He read it three times. Under it, in the queue, there was nothing from her yet.`,
    `At 12:34 he sent the request as next of kin, one line, and sat at the kitchen table to wait for an answer that would take forty two and a half minutes at the very least, and probably until her morning. Over the high bay doors, twenty miles east, in the dark, the clock said 246.`
  ].filter(x=>x!==``);},
